Now, recall that \(u\) is a nonsingular solution of Problem (6.24) if

\[F(u)=0\quad\text{and}\quad DF(u)\quad\text{is an {isomorphism} from $X$ onto $X^{\prime}$.}\]

Hence (6.29) yields:

\[D^{2}J(u)\cdot(w,w)=\langle A^{-1}(DF(u)\cdot w),DF(u)\cdot w\rangle.\] (6.30)

Thus (6.26) implies that

\[D^{2}J(u)\cdot(w,w) \geqslant(\gamma/K^{2})\,\|\,DF(u)\cdot w\,\|_{\star}^{2}\] \[\geqslant\delta\,\|\,w\,\|_{X}^{2}\quad\quad\delta>0,\]

since \(DF(u)\) is an isomorphism of \(X\) onto \(X^{\prime}\). But the mapping \(D^{2}J\) is continuous in \(X\) (because \(F\) is a \(\mathscr{C}^{p}\)-mapping); therefore there exists \(\rho>0\) such that

